 "notes": "Start: p. 19 heading PLATE V., l. 1 ḥā. End: p. 20 last row, Ànnu (l. 13); nuk / Ṭetṭeti / se excluded. Overlines (rubric): p. 19 rows 1-3 entirely (ḥā ... pert 'coming forth.'); row 4 from ànet' to ka; row 5 over Àmentet and àn (line ends over àn). No overlines on p. 20. Line numerals printed mid-word: '2.' inside seχu (given l. 1), '6.' inside ābai-nà (given l. 5), '10.' inside χenrà (given l. 9). p. 20 row 1 has small italic 'ic)' between N35 and the low sign of enma (remnant of a '(sic)'), not a sign. Two figure glyphs recur: (a) hand-to-mouth figure (coded A2; used for Ani's det., seθes, seχu, semaāχeru, ren-k, ut'ā, t'eṭet) and (b) kneeling man with one arm raised, open hand (coded A1 as 1st-person suffix: àm-à, nuk, nà, nuà, àmṭu). The low line with an upright tab at right is coded D36 (ā) throughout (ḥā, āāa, uā, ut'ā, maā groups); the small closed bevelled bar inside the sickle is Aa11. Àusàr is written Q2+D4 (no det.) on p. 19 and l. 7/12, and D4 over Q1+A40 on ll. 8, 9. × at the horned viper's head is part of I9."
